.worktrees/
.tools/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
bin/
# CI and the contributor workflow build the CLI at the repository root.
/twinwright
/twinwright.exe
# What scripts/live-model.sh writes when TW_LIVE_OUT points into the checkout. A
# live-model report and a cassette hold a real model's prompts and answers, and
# the figures worth keeping are quoted in docs/live-model-run.md instead.
live-model-report.json
*.cassette.jsonl
# What `make perf` and `twinwright perf` write by default. A report is one
# machine's measurement; the figures worth keeping are quoted in
# docs/performance.md with the environment block that came with them.
perf.json
# What `make gate` wrote into the repository root before it used a temporary
# directory. A bench report is one run's output, and the baseline it is gated
# against is committed under examples/bench/baselines/.
bench-candidate.json
# The private design workspace: briefs, working specs, implementation plans and a
# progress snapshot. Its own README always said it was ignored while every file in
# it was tracked. Public architectural decisions live in docs/adr/ instead.
/design/
# Scratch for local working notes: scripts, logs and built binaries from a working session.
.superpowers/
